      "id": 38368,
      "name": "flamethrower49",
      "username": "flamethrower49",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-12T21:33:21.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Well, obviously all the villains \"work\" differently, in that they have different&nbsp;flip mechanics, and ways of going about the game.&nbsp;&nbsp;The ultimate goal, however,&nbsp;is the same for most of them - to kill the heroes.&nbsp; So some vague&nbsp;similarities&nbsp;aren't too&nbsp;hard to find, in that respect.</p><p>Ambuscade and Omnitron both employ devices to beat the heroes into submission, for instance.&nbsp; Gloomweaver and Apostate use Relics.&nbsp; Chairman, Gloomweaver, Voss and Dawn each make heavy use of minions of various types.&nbsp; Plague Rat and Spite prefer to work alone.&nbsp; Is that the kind of thing you were talking about?</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:08.204Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
